  "id": "COMPOUND:43064 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "Isoleucic acid, (-)- is consistently identified as a target of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex across three distinct paths, with varying levels of confidence. The first path links Isoleucic acid directly to WIL2-NS, which is then identified as a target of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The second path connects Isoleucic acid to WIL2-NS, which is also a target of Rhodojaponin VII, and ultimately to the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The third path provides a more complex, longer molecular chain, but still identifies WIL2-NS as a target of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. These findings suggest that Isoleucic acid may interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through a common intermediate, WIL2-NS, which is a target of multiple compounds. The evidence supports a potential mechanism where Isoleucic acid influences the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex via WIL2-NS, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
